n-to-george-o-tompkins-between-9-and-15-march-1839-state-of-missouri-v-gates-et-al-for-treason", "series": "JSPPL", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPL4", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppl4-sub02-01", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/legal-records/jsppl4/jsppl4-sub02/jsppl4-sub02-01", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tDocuments Related to<em> State of Missouri v. Gates et al. for Treason</em></p>", "editorialPageNumber": "7", "isPageNumberPresent": false, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54005897/54005897-0007.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3713836188538201352\"><a href=\"#3713836188538201352\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans16\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/elias-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Elias Smith</a> handwriting begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>WE the undersigned being many of us, personally acquainted with the said Joseph Smith jr and the circumstances connected with his imprisonment do concur in the petition &amp; testimony of the above named individuals as most of the transactions therein mentioned we know from personal knowldge to be correctly set forth and from information of others believe the remainder to be true</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17345792159697560333\"><a href=\"#17345792159697560333\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans17\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/elias-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Elias Smith</a> handwriting ends; individual signatories begin.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2607637459989143602\"><a href=\"#2607637459989143602\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per934\" person=\"per934\" title=\"Amasa Mason Lyman\">Amasa Lyman</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Lyman, Amasa Mason\"><p>30 Mar. 1813–4 Feb. 1877. Boatman, gunsmith, farmer. Born at Lyman, Grafton Co., New Hampshire. Son of Roswell Lyman and Martha Mason. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints by Lyman E. Johnson, 27 Apr. 1832. Moved to Hiram, Portage Co....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/amasa-mason-lyman\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13858081506122751266\"><a href=\"#13858081506122751266\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per167\" person=\"per167\" title=\"Henry Garlick Sherwood\">Henry G Sherwood</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Sherwood, Henry Garlick\"><p>20 Apr. 1785–24 Nov. 1867. Surveyor. Born at Kingsbury, Washington Co., New York. Son of Newcomb Sherwood and a woman whose maiden name was Tolman (first name unidentified). Married Polly by 17 May 1823. Lived at Bolton, Warren Co., New York, 1830. Baptized...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/henry-garlick-sherwood\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11786053546126580511\"><a href=\"#11786053546126580511\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per242\" person=\"per242\" title=\"James Newberry\">James Newberry</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Newberry, James\"><p>29 May 1791–10 July 1880. Farmer. Born in Warwick, Orange Co., New York. Son of John Newberry and Jemima Benedict. Married first Mary Smith, 24 Aug. 1811. Moved to Brownhelm, Lorain Co., Ohio, by 1830. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/james-newberry\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16652878106547110957\"><a href=\"#16652878106547110957\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x10248\" person=\"x10248\" title=\"Cyrus Daniels\">Cyrus Daniels</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Daniels, Cyrus\"><p>12 Sept. 1803–before May 1847. Farmer, policeman. Born in Nelson, Chenango Co., New York. Son of Adam Daniels and Phoebe. Moved to Mentor, Geauga Co., Ohio, by 1826. Married Simira Colson, 21 Jan. 1828, in Cuyahoga Co., Ohio. Baptized into Church of Jesus...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/cyrus-daniels\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4331873006520650812\"><a href=\"#4331873006520650812\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per872\" person=\"per872\" title=\"Erastus Snow\">Erastus Snow</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Snow, Erastus\"><p>9 Nov. 1818–27 May 1888. Farmer, teacher, merchant, publisher, manufacturer. Born at St. Johnsbury, Caledonia Co., Vermont. Son of Levi Snow and Lucina Streeter. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints by William Snow, 3 Feb. 1833, at Charleston...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/erastus-snow\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6216201566185070366\"><a href=\"#6216201566185070366\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per131\" person=\"per131\" title=\"Elias Smith\">Elias Smith</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Smith, Elias\"><p>6 Sept. 1804–24 June 1888. Teacher, printer, postmaster, bookkeeper, probate judge, newspaper editor. Born in Royalton, Windsor Co., Vermont. Son of Asahel Smith and Elizabeth Schellenger. Moved to Stockholm, St. Lawrence Co., New York, 1809. Baptized into...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/elias-smith\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">&nbsp;</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\">Joseph Smith Jun<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11736638005412019150\"><a href=\"#11736638005412019150\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans18\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This docket was written vertically at the bottom right corner of the page in unknown handwriting, apparently after the attestation was inscribed and the petition was refolded.</p><hr></div></div></aside> [p. [7]]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3501034225653223738\"><a href=\"#3501034225653223738\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans16\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/elias-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Elias Smith</a> handwriting begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>WE the undersigned being &lt;​many of us​&gt;, personally <span class=\"deleted\">with<